Allow recovery from stalled pod startup

Abandoned launches retained lifecycle locks while retrying readiness
forever, preventing enter and delete from recovering stopped containers.
Silent startup streams could also block deletion of a running container.

Let explicit deletion cancel readiness before acquiring the lifecycle
lock. Cancel queued operations so they cannot recreate the deleted pod.
Propagate readiness cancellation before recreation rebuilds the pod.
Keep CLI disconnection from cancelling background startup. Fail a launch
when its established readiness stream breaks; bound initial connection
attempts and idle reads. Startup heartbeats allow long lifecycle
commands to remain live without an overall setup deadline.

Integration tests cover abandoned launches, stopped containers, explicit
deletion with a paused server, automatic failure without another CLI
command, and healthy setup that outlasts the transport timeout.

Validation: required smoke filters, readiness_wait, and fork_smoke_test
passed via cargo pipeline. The full cargo pipeline --continue run passed
586 tests with two skips and no failures or timeouts.
